From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zedex <zedex@invalid>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 10:07:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] disk: do not read past the end of a CPC image

open_cpc's first pass forces the MFM byte of every track the header
claims - buff[ idx + 0x13 ] - stepping idx through the file by the track
size table, and checks neither that table's zeroes nor the end of the
buffer.  An extended image that says 41 tracks over 40 tracks of data,
with the last size table entry zero for the unformatted track, therefore
reads nineteen bytes past the end of the allocation, and writes there
when that byte happens to be zero.

That is how CPDRead writes a 40 track +3 disk, so real images are
affected: Los 40 Principales Vol. 1 (ZXDB 0014248) is one.  Whether it
faults is whether the byte after the buffer is mapped, so the same image
crashes on one machine and plays on another - on Android, where the
allocator puts a guard page after a large block, it is a reliable
SIGSEGV.

The main loop below already skips unformatted tracks and stops when the
data runs out; this does the same two things.
---
 peripherals/disk/disk.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/peripherals/disk/disk.c b/peripherals/disk/disk.c
index 46f6466..7758e64 100644
--- a/peripherals/disk/disk.c
+++ b/peripherals/disk/disk.c
@@ -1625,6 +1625,13 @@ open_cpc( buffer_t *buffer, disk_t *d, int preindex )
   }
   idx = 256;
   for( i = 0; i < d->sides * d->cylinders; i++ ) {
+    /* An unformatted track has no header to fix up, and a header that claims
+       more tracks than the file carries has no bytes there at all - both of
+       which the main loop below already allows for, and neither of which was
+       checked here. Reading buff[ idx + 0x13 ] past the end of the image is
+       undefined, and where it is a zero byte this writes there too. */
+    if( d->type == DISK_ECPC && tltbl[i] == 0 ) continue;
+    if( idx + 0x13 >= buffer->file.length ) break;
     if( buff[ idx + 0x13 ] == 0 ) /* we now assume MFM */
       buff[ idx + 0x13 ] = 2;
     idx += d->type == DISK_ECPC ? tltbl[i] * 256 : trlen;
